1. नभ् cl. 1. Ā. न॑भते, to burst, be torn or rent asunder, RV. viii, 39, 1; x, 133, 1;
 impf. P. न॑भस्, to break or destroy (?), i, 174, 8 (cf. Dhātup. xviii, 13; Naigh. ii, 19);
 cl. 4. 9. P. नभ्यति, नभ्नाति (Dhātup. xxvi, 130, xxxi, 48), to hurt, injure (pf. Ā. नेभे, Bhaṭṭ.) :
Caus. नभयति, to cause to burst, tear open, AitBr.
